DOLLY 7
PACKAGE rust
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST dso@0
REQUIRES HOST threads@0

# The Rust SDK as rust-build built it. Its rustc finds its sysroot beside
# itself, so /usr/bin/rustc starts it by its own path.
COPY /v0.1.4/demos/rust/Dollyfile-rust-build 8712a7530037ceeadb88c6cb2662b225edf74840aded9746f2334434de01a5c0 /opt/rust-sdk /opt/rust-sdk
COPY /v0.1.4/demos/rust/Dollyfile-rust-build 8712a7530037ceeadb88c6cb2662b225edf74840aded9746f2334434de01a5c0 /usr/share/licenses/rust /usr/share/licenses/rust
# rustc links what it compiles with the C toolchain.
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-cc d84ac9e974b50e7dcb2a4e3a9ddbc1290f0c00f137bdb79802df10daf9f000df
FILE /usr/bin/rustc
    #!/bin/slop
    /opt/rust-sdk/bin/rustc "$@"
FILE /usr/bin/rustdoc
    #!/bin/slop
    /opt/rust-sdk/bin/rustdoc "$@"
EXPORTS TOOL rustc
EXPORTS TOOL rustdoc
EXPORTS FOLDER rust-sdk /opt/rust-sdk
EXPORTS FOLDER rust-licenses /usr/share/licenses/rust
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/rustc.1
    rustc: the Rust compiler and standard library, built inside Dolly from their
    pinned sources (Rust 1.98.1, its LLVM 22.1.8).
    
      rustc main.rs -o main     compiles a program; cc links it
      rustdoc --test lib.rs     runs a library's doc tests
      cargo build               builds a crate (the cargo package)
    
    Panics unwind, by WebAssembly exceptions; a crate built with panic = "abort"
    links the same library. There are no dynamic Rust libraries. Executables
    link threaded and need threads@0 in the image that runs them. The compiler loads procedural macros, so an image that keeps
    rustc declares dso@0. Upstream's documentation: https://doc.rust-lang.org/
